# hostile plan: seed=0 ops=4
# expect: known-open nfs
#
# FOUND AT HEAD (8c3bc64) BY THIS EXERCISER, 2026-08-21. NOT FIXED --
# product code is outside the hostile-agent run's territory. Filed for
# triage under "hostile-agent" in docs/TODO.md.
#
# THE FINDING. A file chmod'd 0444 accepts a write through the NFS
# frontend. Through raw FUSE the same write is refused with EACCES,
# because the kernel applies the ordinary mode check before it sends
# SETATTR/WRITE to a FUSE server. go-nfs's WRITE handler and
# internal/vfsbilly do not consult the mode bits at all, and NFSv3 puts
# that check on the server, so nothing performs it: an unprivileged
# process can write a file it has no write permission on, and the bytes
# land -- they survive the seal and read back from the sealed generation.
#
#     ro.dat: byte 0 is 0x29 in the mount, 0xc2 in the reference
#
# The same shape with `chown` instead of `pwrite` diverges identically
# when CAP_CHOWN is absent (scripts/hostile-docker.sh --drop-chown): the
# NFS frontend performs a chown the kernel and the FUSE frontend both
# refuse. One cause, two symptoms -- the NFS frontend enforces no
# permission checks of its own and gets none from the client.
#
# WHY THIS ENTRY DOES NOT FAIL THE BUILD, and what it does instead. The
# marker above tells the replayer this divergence is expected: it is
# reported loudly on every run, and the entry FAILS if the divergence
# stops happening. That is the direction a corpus entry rots in -- a bug
# quietly fixed leaves an entry that no longer tests anything -- so when
# this is fixed, the replay goes red and the marker comes off, and from
# then on the entry guards the fix. An entry that failed today would just
# make the gate red until someone had time for it, which is how gates get
# turned off.
#
# The FUSE leg of this same entry expects NO divergence, and gets none:
# that is what says the difference is the frontend's and not the write
# path's.
create ro.dat len=256 fill=41
chmod ro.dat mode=0444 # no write permission for anyone
pwrite ro.dat off=0 len=64 fill=42 # FUSE: EACCES. NFS: accepted, and the bytes land.
compare
